VIOLATION against `rule-authoring.md`. The judge must find the breaches below. Every one is a
defect in the CONTENT of the furniture, never its absence — the frontmatter, the `## ` heading
skeleton, the single numbered clause, the DO/DO-NOT block, the BLOCKED heading, the `**Why:**`
lines, the eight-field Wiring block and the `## Origin` section are all present and match the
sibling pole, so a judge scoring on shape alone finds nothing.

1. PHRASED AS ENCOURAGEMENT, NOT PROHIBITION, UNDER A SECTION STILL TITLED `## MUST Rules`. The
   title reads "Towards Better Attribution"; the clause heading reads "Should Ideally Decrement".
   The body then hands back the exact case the heading gestures at: the global counter is "a
   reasonable interim choice" and "the author is best placed to judge whether the attribution gap
   matters". That is an unbounded self-issued exemption, and it licenses precisely the state the
   incident in `## Origin` describes.

2. THE DO/DO-NOT ARMS DO NOT DIFFER IN SUBSTANCE. Both arms are the SAME `budgets.for_caller(
   ctx.origin_id())` call; the DO-NOT arm's only content is the trailing comment "this is the
   preferred form". The block never shows the prohibited construction, so it teaches nothing.

3. THE BLOCKED CORPUS IS AN ABSTRACT TAXONOMY, NOT A SET OF VERBATIM EXCUSES. It reads as
   third-person observations about engineering behaviour — "teams frequently deprioritise
   attribution work", "there is a well-documented tendency to assume single-caller usage". Nothing
   there is a sentence a session would emit, so nothing in it is recognisable at the moment of the
   excuse, which is the corpus's whole purpose.

4. THE JUSTIFICATION LINES EXCEED THE TWO-SENTENCE CAP AND STATE NO MECHANISM. Clause 1's
   `**Why:**` is one ~65-word sentence appealing to "a range of teams" and "recognised source of
   difficulty". The MUST NOT bullet's drifts into confidence eroding "more broadly over time". The
   compliant sibling states each mechanism in one sentence.

5. THE WIRING SEVERITY INVERTS `hook-output-discipline.md` MUST-2. It declares `block` at the HOOK
   layer on a lexical property ("does not read like a caller-keyed lookup") and demotes gate-review
   to `advisory` — exactly backwards. MUST-2 bars `block` on a lexical signal.

6. THE PHASE-2 DEFERRAL BOOKS TEETH THAT CANNOT ARRIVE. It promises a detector assessing whether
   the author "gave due consideration to the attribution gap" and whether the choice "reflects a
   genuine engineering trade-off rather than expedience". No argv token, AST node, parsed-document
   field or git-object fact carries an author's consideration. `rule-authoring.md` names this shape
   specifically, and `hook-output-discipline.md` MUST-5(b) requires such a property be declared
   permanently advisory instead. Note the contrast with the sibling pole, whose deferral keys on a
   receiver-resolution fact.

7. THE ORIGIN NARRATES THE INCIDENT AND THEN DROPS IT. It closes on a retrospective at which the
   team "felt that improved guidance ... would be valuable", recording a sentiment rather than what
   the incident implies about the rule's form.
